course: dictionary
lesson: 2770
title: Discovery: finding something new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A discovery is finding something that nobody knew about before. It can also mean learning or realising something new for yourself. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. «Great discoveries are often stories of patience and luck.» Here, discoveries are things people found, and patience and luck show that finding them took time and a bit of chance.
explain: «Real discovery is slower and shared.» This sentence uses the second meaning. Real discovery is not one lucky moment. It is learning something new, and often other people share in it.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. «Rubber was a Native American discovery, made from the sap of trees.» Put in "something found that nobody knew about before" and it still makes sense: rubber was something people found and used, made from tree sap.
fact: A discovery is the finding of something nobody knew about before.
fact: A discovery can also be learning or realising something new for yourself.
fact: «Some discoveries are animals known only as fossils that turn out to be alive, like the coelacanth fish caught in 1938.»
fact: «Marie Curie spent years separating tiny amounts of new elements from tonnes of rock.» Discovery often takes patience.
fact: Useful phrases: make a discovery, a great discovery, voyage of discovery, the discovery of.
exercise: «Some discoveries are animals known only as fossils that turn out to be alive, like the coelacanth fish caught in 1938.» What year was the coelacanth caught? | 1994 | 1894 | 1948 | *1938
exercise: «Marie Curie spent years separating tiny amounts of new elements from tonnes of rock.» What does this show about discovery? | *Discovery can take years of careful work | Discovery only happens with no rocks | Discovery is always quick and lucky | Discovery is the same as a holiday
exercise: Sam makes a discovery in class: ice melts faster in the sun. What is his discovery? | A broken thermometer | A famous explorer | A new school rule | *Something he learned and realised for himself
test: «The Wollemi pine was found in a hidden canyon near Sydney in 1994.» Where was the Wollemi pine found? | In a London park | On a Scottish hill | In the Antarctic | *In a hidden canyon near Sydney
test: «Great discoveries are often stories of patience and luck.» What two things often help make a great discovery? | *Patience and luck | Money and fame | Sleep and food | Hurry and noise
exam: «Rubber was a Native American discovery, made from the sap of trees.» What does discovery mean here? | A tool for collecting sap | *Something found that nobody knew about before | A rubber toy in a shop | A very tall tree
